Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 03:11:42 +0700
Subject: [PATCH] SourbyCraft - one clear line for a legacy plugin refused
 while the bridge is off

FileProviderSource skips a jar whose plugin declares neither folia-supported nor canvas-supported and that the Aurora Bridge did not admit (aurora.bridge.mode = off) with one WARN naming the setting, and records it for /plugins, instead of the provider factory's 'Error loading plugin' ERROR and stack trace. The factories keep their refusal as the backstop.

diff --git a/src/main/java/io/papermc/paper/plugin/provider/source/FileProviderSource.java b/src/main/java/io/papermc/paper/plugin/provider/source/FileProviderSource.java
index 9661f033bbb2c00073f1c891e1411c2a9943a37a..1ccd3913810a017c74022515904a5c428ddbc5aa 100644
--- a/src/main/java/io/papermc/paper/plugin/provider/source/FileProviderSource.java
+++ b/src/main/java/io/papermc/paper/plugin/provider/source/FileProviderSource.java
@@ -81,6 +81,12 @@ public class FileProviderSource implements ProviderSource<Path, Path> {
             return;
         }
 
+        // SourbyCraft start - Aurora Bridge: a plugin refused for missing folia-supported (mode off) gets one clear line, not a stack trace
+        if (!config.isFoliaSupported() && !dev.iyanz.sourbycraft.bridge.AuroraBridge.admitLegacy(config.getName())) {
+            dev.iyanz.sourbycraft.bridge.AuroraBridge.refused(config.getName(), config.getDisplayName(), context.getFileName().toString());
+            return;
+        }
+        // SourbyCraft end - Aurora Bridge
         type.register(entrypointHandler, file, context);
     }
 
